"content": "engenn5le01ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to spill ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to allow a liquid to leave a container without intention", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I feel really bad I spilled coffee on your assistant.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le01ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use at work.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "assistant", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who helps another person in an office", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Is your assistant angry that I spilled coffee?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le01ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "efficient", "type": "name"}, {"content": "works quickly and accurately", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You are an efficient worker.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le01ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "educational outreach", "type": "name"}, {"content": "communications designed to train or teach the public", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You will be responsible for educational outreach.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le01ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "blog", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an electronic journal ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You'll write blogs and articles for the company website. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le01ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "focus group", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a meeting organized by a business to understand people's opinions", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You'll also plan focus group sessions.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le01ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Simple Past Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use the Simple Past tense to talk about events that are finished.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Simple Past tense verbs can be regular or irregular.<br/> Regular verbs end in <span class=\"strong\">-ed</span> or <span class=\"strong\">-ied</span>.<br/> Irregular verbs change in different ways.<br/> For questions in the past, you use the auxiliary <span class=\"italic\">did</span> followed by the verb in the base form, like <span class=\"italic\">Did you ask ... ?</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">Did</span> is the past form of <span class=\"italic\">to do</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":9,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Past Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to spill \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"spilled\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to copy\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"copied\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to protect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"protected\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to lose\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"lost\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was, were\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"had\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to speak \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"spoke\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to think\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"thought\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I had problems last week. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I didn't finish the report on time.<span class=\"prelo-letter-page-break\"></span>", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Future Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Future tense to talk about actions in the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The auxiliary <span class=\"strong\">will</span> goes before the verb. The short form is <span class=\"strong\">'ll.</span><br/><br/>You use the Future tense when you talk about intentions, make offers or make predictions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I will finish the project soon. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You will be responsible for educational outreach.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We'll send the invitations.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Listen to the songs \"I Will Always Love You\" by Whitney Houston and \"I Will Survive\" by Gloria Gaynor online.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Print and read the lyrics of each song.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Underline the examples of the Future tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With a partner, discuss which song you prefer and explain why.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I listen to two English songs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I listen for sentences about the future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss the songs with a partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn5le01ob09re2img05.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn5le01ob09re2img05.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Mr. Warren</span>:  Please come in, Peter.  How are you doing? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:  I'm good, thanks, Mr. Warren, I know I had problems last week ...<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mr. Warren</span>:  Peter ...<br>"}, {"image": "engenn5le01ob09re2img08.jpg", "time": "7000", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:  I'm sorry I didn't finish the report on time ...<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mr. Warren</span>:  Oh Peter, that's OK.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:  And I'm sorry I lost Amanda's document ...<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mr. Warren</span>:  Peter ... <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: And I feel really bad I spilled coffee on your assistant and arrived late ...<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mr. Warren</span>:  Peter ...  please let me speak.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:  Yes?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mr. Warren</span>:  You are a good worker. You are friendly and efficient. I'm giving you a promotion. <br>"}, {"image": "engenn5le01ob09re2img01.jpg", "time": "25000", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:  Really?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mr. Warren</span>:  Yes. As of Monday, you will be responsible for educational outreach.\nYou'll write blogs and articles for the company website. You'll also plan focus group sessions. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Cool! Thank you, Mr. Warren!<br>"}], "audiosrc": "engenn5le01ob09re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le01ob09re2img05.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "  I can talk about jobs and work. ", "type": "Learn